# Project Charter

## Project Name

AI-Enabled Retail Energy Business Intelligence

---

## Project Purpose

The purpose of this project is to explore how modern business intelligence,
data engineering, data quality practices, automation, and artificial
intelligence can improve decision-making within the retail energy sector.

The project will develop an open-source BI framework using publicly available
and synthetic data.

---

## Background

Retail energy organizations operate in a highly data-intensive environment.

Business users need to understand customer consumption, product performance,
market conditions, revenue, margin, and portfolio trends.

Traditional reporting provides visibility into historical performance.
However, modern BI can extend beyond reporting by combining:

- Reliable data pipelines
- Governed business metrics
- Dimensional data modeling
- Data quality monitoring
- Interactive dashboards
- AI-assisted development
- AI-assisted decision support

This project explores how these capabilities can work together within a
retail energy context.

---

## Primary Goal

Build a reusable BI framework that transforms retail energy data into
reliable, understandable, and actionable business intelligence.

---

## Business Objectives

The project aims to:

1. Establish a reliable retail energy data pipeline.
2. Develop a reusable analytical data model.
3. Define standardized and governed business metrics.
4. Build interactive BI dashboards.
5. Monitor data quality and pipeline health.
6. Explore AI-assisted BI development.
7. Explore AI-assisted business insight generation.
8. Establish a foundation for future advanced analytics.

